      "concept": "CSR and system-instruction legality decision",
      "security objective": "Integrity",
      "reasoning": "The module explicitly computes whether a CSR/system access is permitted and whether the current instruction is legal. csr_check derives csr_valid from the addressed CSR, write form, debug-mode status, privilege, and counter-enable restrictions at lines 659-744; illegal_check then decides illegal_cmd from opcode/funct fields and csr_valid at lines 752-820; and trap_ctrl.instr_il turns that decision into an illegal-instruction exception in EX_EXECUTE or EX_ALU_WAIT at lines 825-826, which trap_buffer records in trap_ctrl.exc_buf at line 899. Integrity is Established because these decisions control whether disallowed CSR/system operations are rejected by trap rather than executed.",
